XXI. 🧬 CROSS-CITADEL EVENT

A cross-Citadel interaction must retain both identities:

A-W₁
   │
   │ diplomatic event
   ▼
B-W₇

The resulting event must not imply:

A-W₁ became B-W₇

Instead:

SOURCE = A-W₁
TARGET = B-W₇
EVENT = Eₓ

This preserves domain sovereignty.


---

XXII. 🌐 FEDERATED WATERMARK

If reconciliation creates a new shared state:

A-W₁
B-W₇
   │
   ▼
RECONCILIATION
   │
   ▼
F-W₁

then:

F-W₁

is a new proof anchor.

It does not replace:

A-W₁
B-W₇

Therefore:

SHARED STATE DOES NOT DESTROY SOURCE HISTORY.


