II. 🗣️ THE AMBASSADOR

Canonical object:

pub struct Ambassador {
    pub ambassador_id: AmbassadorId,
    pub principal_citadel: CitadelId,
    pub mandate_id: DiplomaticMandateId,
    pub authority_scope: DiplomaticScope,
    pub appointed_at: Timestamp,
    pub expires_at: Option<Timestamp>,
    pub identity_proof: IdentityProofId,
    pub mandate_proof: MandateProofId,
    pub signature: Signature,
}

An Ambassador is therefore not simply a person, process, or AI agent carrying a title.

The constitutional fact is:

AMBASSADOR
=
IDENTITY
+
MANDATE
+
SCOPE
+
TEMPORAL VALIDITY
+
PROOF


---

III. 🔐 DIPLOMATIC MANDATE

An Ambassador may only act within an explicit mandate.

pub struct DiplomaticMandate {
    pub mandate_id: DiplomaticMandateId,
    pub principal: CitadelId,
    pub permitted_actions: DiplomaticScope,
    pub prohibited_actions: DiplomaticScope,
    pub valid_from: Timestamp,
    pub valid_until: Option<Timestamp>,
    pub evidence_root: EvidenceRoot,
    pub signature: Signature,
}

The critical distinction:

REPRESENTATION IS NOT SOVEREIGNTY.

An Ambassador represents a Citadel.

The Ambassador does not become the Citadel.


---

IV. ⚖️ MANDATE BOUNDARIES

A mandate might authorize:

DISCUSS
NEGOTIATE
PROPOSE
EXCHANGE_EVIDENCE
REQUEST_RECOGNITION
REQUEST_TRUST
PROPOSE_ACCORD

but explicitly prohibit:

ALTER_CONSTITUTION
TRANSFER_SOVEREIGNTY
GRANT_UNAUTHORIZED_AUTHORITY
DELETE_HISTORY
REWRITE_WATERMARK
OVERRIDE_LOCAL_RULESET
COMMIT_UNAUTHORIZED_OPERATION

This creates a constitutional perimeter around diplomacy.


---

