VI. 📜 ACCORD OBJECT

pub struct ConstitutionalAccord {
    pub accord_id: AccordId,
    pub parties: Vec<CitadelId>,
    pub negotiated_by: Vec<AmbassadorId>,
    pub scope: AccordScope,
    pub obligations_root: ObligationRoot,
    pub evidence_root: EvidenceRoot,
    pub challenge_status: ChallengeStatus,
    pub verification_status: VerificationStatus,
    pub effective_watermark: WatermarkId,
    pub signatures: Vec<Signature>,
}

An Accord is therefore a constitutional relationship object.


---

VII. 🤝 ACCORD ≠ TREATY OF ABSORPTION

An Accord may establish:

mutual recognition
evidence exchange
shared protocol
federated operation
limited authority delegation
joint verification

It does not automatically establish:

common sovereignty
common constitution
common identity
common history

Unless those are separately and explicitly established.


---

VIII. 🧭 ACCORD SCOPE

pub enum AccordScope {
    Recognition,
    EvidenceExchange,
    DiplomaticCommunication,
    Research,
    Federation,
    OperationalInteroperation,
    LimitedDelegation,
}

Scope is explicit.

Therefore:

RESEARCH

cannot silently become:

OPERATIONAL_INTEROPERATION

and:

OPERATIONAL_INTEROPERATION

cannot silently become:

SOVEREIGN_AUTHORITY


