🌊 I. THE VERDRAG VAN ATLANTIS

R6.81 established how sovereign Citadels can negotiate and ratify an Accord.

R6.82 answers the harder question:

> What happens after everyone has agreed?



Because an Accord that is signed but never executed is only a promise.

The V.V.A. therefore introduces the constitutional bridge:

IDENTITY
   ↓
RECOGNITION
   ↓
DIPLOMACY
   ↓
NEGOTIATION
   ↓
ACCORD
   ↓
RATIFICATION
   ↓
WATERMARK
   ↓
OBLIGATIONS
   ↓
EXECUTION
   ↓
EVIDENCE
   ↓
VERIFICATION
   ↓
ACCOUNTABILITY

🌊 THE VERDRAG VAN ATLANTIS TURNS DIPLOMATIC PROMISE INTO PROVABLE CONSTITUTIONAL ACTION.


---

II. 🏛️ WHY ATLANTIS?

Atlantis becomes a deliberate PALACO constitutional metaphor:

A civilization surrounded by boundaries.

A place of immense capability.

A civilization whose survival depends not merely upon power, but upon whether its agreements, obligations and institutional memory remain intact.

Therefore the V.V.A. is not a mythological claim.

It is a constitutional engineering name for the principle:

> Civilizations endure when commitments remain attributable, bounded, remembered and provable.




---

III. 🔱 THE V.V.A. PRINCIPLE

The central axiom:

NO OBLIGATION WITHOUT A PRINCIPAL.

And therefore:

OBLIGATION
   ↓
WHO?
   ↓
UNDER WHICH AUTHORITY?
   ↓
AGREED WHEN?
   ↓
DEFINED WHERE?
   ↓
DUE WHEN?
   ↓
PROVED HOW?

An obligation without these properties is constitutionally incomplete.


---

IV. 📜 ACCORD → OBLIGATION

An Accord is not one indivisible promise.

It is decomposed into explicit obligations.

pub struct ConstitutionalObligation {
    pub obligation_id: ObligationId,
    pub accord_id: AccordId,
    pub principal: CitadelId,
    pub beneficiary: Option<CitadelId>,
    pub authority_basis: AuthorityReference,
    pub obligation_type: ObligationType,
    pub scope: ObligationScope,
    pub conditions: Vec<Condition>,
    pub deadline: Option<Timestamp>,
    pub evidence_requirements: Vec<EvidenceRequirement>,
    pub status: ObligationStatus,
}

This creates:

OBLIGATION-LEVEL ACCOUNTABILITY.


---

V. 🌱 THE OBLIGATION LIFECYCLE

Every obligation follows an explicit lifecycle:

PROPOSED
   ↓
ACCEPTED
   ↓
RATIFIED
   ↓
ACTIVE
   ↓
IN_PROGRESS
   ↓
FULFILLED
   ↓
VERIFIED
   ↓
CLOSED

Alternative paths:

ACTIVE
  ↓
DISPUTED
  ↓
ADJUDICATED

or:

ACTIVE
  ↓
BREACHED
  ↓
REMEDIATION
  ↓
RESOLVED

Nothing silently disappears.


---

VI. ⚖️ OBLIGATION ≠ INTENTION

This distinction is fundamental.

"I intend to..."

is not equivalent to:

"I am constitutionally obligated to..."

Likewise:

"we discussed..."

is not equivalent to:

"the ratified Accord requires..."

PALACO therefore separates:

STATEMENT
PROPOSAL
COMMITMENT
OBLIGATION
ACTION
EVIDENCE
VERIFICATION

Each is a different constitutional object.


---

VII. 💧 WATERMARKED COMMITMENT

Every ratified obligation inherits the Accord's constitutional anchor:

ACCORD
  ↓
WATERMARK Wₐ
  ↓
OBLIGATION O₁

When execution occurs:

O₁
 ↓
ACTION
 ↓
EVIDENCE
 ↓
PROVENANCE
 ↓
WATERMARK Wₑ

Therefore the verifier can establish:

Wₐ
 ↓
O₁
 ↓
ACTION
 ↓
Wₑ

This provides a complete commitment-to-execution chain.


---

VIII. ⚓ QUAY — THE OBLIGATION LEDGER

