No state is rewritten.

The constitutional lineage is:

STATE₀ → STATE₁ → STATE₂ → STATE₃ → STATE₄ → STATE₅


---

XXII. ⚖️ RESTORATIVE JUSTICE PRINCIPLE

PALACO therefore avoids two dangerous extremes:

Extreme A — Forgetfulness

> “The breach is forgiven, so erase it.”



❌ Rejected.

Extreme B — Permanent Punishment

> “The breach occurred, so restoration is impossible.”



❌ Not universally required.

PALACO instead establishes:

ACCOUNTABILITY + MEMORY + CORRECTION + POSSIBILITY OF RESTORATION


---

XXIII. 🔐 AUTHORITY REDUCTION

Where a breach demonstrates that existing authority was too broad, remediation may produce:

AUTHORITY₁
   ↓
BREACH
   ↓
REVIEW
   ↓
AUTHORITY₂ < AUTHORITY₁

This is not necessarily punishment.

It can be constitutional risk correction.


---

XXIV. 🌐 FEDERATION SAFETY

If a federated Citadel breaches a material obligation:

FEDERATION
   ↓
BREACH
   ↓
LOCAL CONTAINMENT
   ↓
FEDERATED REVIEW

The federation must not automatically punish unrelated members.

Responsibility remains attributable.

Therefore:

COLLECTIVE RELATIONSHIP ≠ COLLECTIVE GUILT.


---

XXV. 🧭 DIPLOMATIC RESTORATION ACCORD

Restoration may itself produce a new Accord:

V.V.A.
 ↓
BREACH
 ↓
REMEDIATION ACCORD
 ↓
VERIFICATION
 ↓
RESTORATION ACCORD

The restoration instrument therefore becomes independently auditable.


---

XXVI. ☄️ THE FOUR GREAT STATES

PALACO now distinguishes:

TRUST
   ↓
BREACH
   ↓
REMEDIATION
   ↓
RESTORATION

These are not merely emotional or diplomatic states.

They are cryptographically attributable constitutional states.


---

XXVII. 🔱 R6.83 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

R6.83-I01
A breach SHALL be attributable to a specific obligation.

R6.83-I02
A breach claim SHALL remain distinct from a verified breach.

R6.83-I03
A breach SHALL require evidence.

R6.83-I04
A breach SHALL remain challengeable.

R6.83-I05
