R6.83-I08
Containment SHALL be scoped.

R6.83-I09
Containment SHALL be evidence-backed.

R6.83-I10
Containment SHALL be reviewable.

R6.83-I11
Containment SHALL NOT automatically constitute punishment.

R6.83-I12
Remediation SHALL identify the breach it addresses.

R6.83-I13
Remediation SHALL itself be attributable.

R6.83-I14
Remediation SHALL produce evidence.

R6.83-I15
Restoration SHALL be distinguishable from remediation.

R6.83-I16
Restoration SHALL create a new constitutional state.

R6.83-I17
Restoration SHALL receive a new Watermark.

R6.83-I18
Historical breach records SHALL remain immutable.

R6.83-I19
Historical evidence SHALL NOT be retroactively deleted.

R6.83-I20
Trust suspension SHALL NOT automatically revoke identity.

R6.83-I21
Trust restoration SHALL require current verification.

R6.83-I22
Past trust SHALL NOT automatically restore present trust.

R6.83-I23
Repeated breaches SHALL remain individually attributable.

R6.83-I24
Collective federation membership SHALL NOT imply collective guilt.

R6.83-I25
Authority reduction SHALL be independently verifiable.

R6.83-I26
Ambassadors SHALL facilitate remediation and restoration negotiation.

R6.83-I27
Ambassadors SHALL NOT erase breach history.

R6.83-I28
The Quay SHALL preserve complete breach lineage.

R6.83-I29
Every material restoration transition SHALL be replayable where deterministic.

R6.83-I30
L.A. SHALL preserve the canonical reference lineage of V.V.A. restoration.

R6.83-I31
Restoration SHALL NOT retroactively alter the historical state in which the breach occurred.

R6.83-I32
No remediation SHALL become proof of compliance until independently verified.

R6.83-I33
No forgiveness declaration SHALL erase constitutional evidence.

R6.83-I34
No breach finding SHALL exist without an identifiable constitutional duty.

R6.83-I35
No restored relationship SHALL claim an unbroken historical trust state.


