R6.96-I13
A declaration of finality SHALL NOT itself establish valid finality.

R6.96-I14
Procedural finality SHALL remain distinguishable from historical truth.

R6.96-I15
Historical truth SHALL remain distinguishable from contemporary determination.

R6.96-I16
A determination SHALL be evaluated against evidence available within its relevant temporal context.

R6.96-I17
Later evidence SHALL NOT silently contaminate the historical reconstruction of earlier decision contexts.

R6.96-I18
Reopened determinations SHALL preserve the reason for reopening.

R6.96-I19
Superseded determinations SHALL remain replayable where material.

R6.96-I20
No finality mechanism SHALL create authority beyond its defined scope.

R6.96-I21
No successor state SHALL masquerade as the uninterrupted predecessor state.

R6.96-I22
Constitutional finality SHALL remain attributable, traceable and replayable.


