XVII. 🔒 R6.102 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

R6.102-I01
Material constitutional relationships SHALL be explicitly typed.

R6.102-I02
Lineage SHALL remain distinguishable from general relation.

R6.102-I03
Material relations SHALL possess an identifiable basis.

R6.102-I04
A relation SHALL NOT be inferred solely from proximity or similarity.

R6.102-I05
Material relation claims SHALL be evidence-linked where required.

R6.102-I06
Temporal authority SHALL impose temporal validity on dependent relations where applicable.

R6.102-I07
Expired authority SHALL NOT silently remain active through stale relations.

R6.102-I08
BRAINPOWER MAY discover and model relationships but SHALL NOT autonomously authorize them.

R6.102-I09
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge material graph relationships.

R6.102-I10
TRIAS SHALL verify material authority-bearing relations.

R6.102-I11
Material graph transitions SHALL be watermarkable.

R6.102-I12
Quay SHALL preserve the provenance underlying material graph transitions.

R6.102-I13
Historical graph states SHALL remain reconstructible.

R6.102-I14
Graph evolution SHALL NOT retroactively rewrite prior graph states.

R6.102-I15
Orphan nodes SHALL remain explicitly identifiable.

R6.102-I16
Orphan edges SHALL remain explicitly identifiable.

R6.102-I17
Unknown relationships SHALL remain distinguishable from false relationships.

R6.102-I18
Conflicting relationships SHALL remain distinguishable from absent relationships.

R6.102-I19
Material dependencies SHALL be replayable where required.

R6.102-I20
The constitutional forest SHALL support continuous evolution without historical erasure.


