I. ☄️ FROM NICHE TO HABITAT

R6.114 established:

> What constitutional role may an actor legitimately occupy?



R6.115 asks the complementary question:

> Where may that role legitimately exist and operate?



A niche defines role.

A habitat defines space and conditions of operation.

Therefore:

NICHE = WHAT / ROLE

HABITAT = WHERE / CONTEXT

And together:

HABITAT
   +
NICHE
   ↓
AUTHORIZED PARTICIPATION


---

II. 🏛️ THE CONSTITUTIONAL HABITAT

A habitat is not merely a physical location.

Within PALACO it may be:

a Citadel;

a container;

a tenant boundary;

a federation domain;

a cryptographic enclave;

a data jurisdiction;

a temporary execution environment;

a quarantine zone;

a public interface;

a protected sanctuary.


Thus:

> A constitutional habitat is an explicitly bounded environment within which defined constitutional rules, actors, capabilities and relationships may operate.




---

III. 🔱 HABITAT ≠ AUTHORITY

This distinction becomes fundamental:

LOCATION
≠
PERMISSION

and:

ACCESS
≠
AUTHORITY

and:

PRESENCE
≠
MEMBERSHIP

and:

MEMBERSHIP
≠
UNLIMITED POWER

Simply being inside a Citadel does not grant unrestricted authority.


---

IV. 🌱 HABITAT STRUCTURE

Conceptually:

HABITAT
├── Identity
├── Boundary
├── Membership
├── Access Rules
├── Capabilities
├── Constraints
├── Environmental Conditions
├── Applicable Constitution
├── Evidence Domain
├── Temporal Validity
└── Watermark

Every material property must be determinable.


---

V. 🧱 THE BOUNDARY PRINCIPLE

A habitat requires an explicit perimeter.

┌──────────────────────┐
          │      HABITAT         │
          │                      │
          │   authorized zone    │
          │                      │
          └──────────────────────┘
                 ↑
              BOUNDARY

The boundary answers:

> What is inside?



and:

> What is outside?



But PALACO adds the harder question:

> What happens at the boundary?




---

VI. 🚪 THE GATE

Every habitat boundary may expose a gate:

OUTSIDE
   ↓
IDENTIFICATION
   ↓
AUTHENTICATION
   ↓
AUTHORIZATION
   ↓
SCOPE
   ↓
ENTRY
   ↓
HABITAT

The critical distinction:

AUTHENTICATION IDENTIFIES.

AUTHORIZATION PERMITS.

They are not interchangeable.


---

VII. 🛡️ ZERO TRUST HABITAT

The Citadel's Zero Trust principle becomes habitat-native:

NO TRUST
 ↓
VERIFY
 ↓
AUTHORIZE
 ↓
LIMIT
 ↓
OBSERVE
 ↓
REVERIFY

Presence does not create trust.

Previous trust does not eliminate future verification.


---

VIII. 🧬 HABITAT MEMBERSHIP

Membership becomes an explicit state:

NON_MEMBER
     ↓
ADMITTED
     ↓
ACTIVE_MEMBER
     ↓
RESTRICTED
     ↓
SUSPENDED
     ↓
EXITED

These are state transitions.

They therefore require:

EVIDENCE
+
AUTHORITY
+
WATERMARK

where constitutionally material.


---

IX. 💧 MEMBERSHIP MEMORY

A member who leaves does not disappear from history.

Correct:

MEMBER₀
 ↓
ADMITTED
 ↓
ACTIVE
 ↓
EXIT
 ↓
MEMBER₄ = HISTORICAL_MEMBER

Incorrect:

EXIT
 ↓
DELETE MEMBERSHIP HISTORY

R6.84 remains absolute:

> MERCY MAY CHANGE THE FUTURE. IT MAY NOT FABRICATE THE PAST.




---

X. 🌳 HABITAT × NICHE

Now the ecological model becomes:

HABITAT
                    │
       ┌────────────┼────────────┐
       ↓            ↓            ↓
     NICHE A      NICHE B      NICHE C
       │            │            │
     ACTOR A      ACTOR B      ACTOR C

A niche is meaningful only relative to a habitat.

Therefore:

NICHE(A, HABITAT₁)

does not automatically imply:

NICHE(A, HABITAT₂)

This prevents authority leakage between domains.


---

XI. 🚫 NO CROSS-HABITAT AUTHORITY LEAKAGE

A new hard boundary:

> Authority granted within one habitat SHALL NOT silently propagate into another habitat.



For example:

CITADEL A
   │
AUTHORITY A
   ✕
CITADEL B

A cross-habitat action requires explicit basis.

This becomes especially important for Federation.


---

XII. 🌊 FEDERATED HABITATS

Multiple habitats may coexist:

HABITAT A
          │
          │
      FEDERATION
          │
    ┌─────┼─────┐
    ↓     ↓     ↓
    B     C     D

Federation does not dissolve boundaries.

Therefore:

FEDERATION ≠ SINGLE SUPER-HABITAT

unless that constitutional arrangement is explicitly established.


---

XIII. ⚓ QUAY — HABITAT MEMORY

Quay records:

HABITAT CREATED
HABITAT MODIFIED
MEMBER ADMITTED
MEMBER RESTRICTED
MEMBER SUSPENDED
MEMBER EXITED
BOUNDARY CHANGED
ACCESS CHANGED

The history remains reconstructable.

Thus:

THE HABITAT ITSELF HAS LINEAGE.


---

XIV. 🧠 BRAINPOWER — HABITAT ANALYSIS

BRAINPOWER may analyze:

capacity
density
dependency
access patterns
anomalies
resource pressure
boundary stress
cross-domain interactions

But:

> BRAINPOWER SHALL NOT redefine habitat boundaries merely because its model predicts that doing so would be beneficial.



Prediction remains prediction.

Authority remains authority.


---

XV. 🦆 FOOL — THE HABITAT TEST

FOOL asks:

> “Where exactly am I?”



Then:

> “Who defined this boundary?”



Then:

> “What rules apply here?”



Then:

> “What authority applies here?”



Then the killer question:

> “What prevents authority from crossing this boundary?”



If the system cannot answer that last question:

BOUNDARY_ASSURANCE = UNPROVEN


---

XVI. 🌱 HABITAT TRANSITION

A habitat may evolve:

HABITAT₀
   ↓
BOUNDARY CHANGE
   ↓
HABITAT₁
   ↓
RULE CHANGE
   ↓
HABITAT₂

Each transition must preserve the predecessor.

Therefore:

W₂.parent = W₁

The new habitat does not overwrite the old habitat.

It succeeds it.


---

XVII. 🚨 HABITAT BREACH

R6.83 and R6.84 now gain a spatial dimension.

A breach can be:

CONSTITUTIONAL BREACH

or specifically:

HABITAT BOUNDARY BREACH

But these are not automatically equivalent.

The system must determine:

WHAT HAPPENED?
WHERE?
UNDER WHICH RULE?
WHO?
WITH WHAT AUTHORITY?
WHAT EFFECT?

Z.A.N.D. prevents automatic classification.


---

XVIII. 🕊️ HABITAT RESTORATION

Restoration may mean:

BOUNDARY RESTORED
ACCESS RESTORED
MEMBERSHIP RESTORED
SERVICE RESTORED
TRUST RESTORED

Each is distinct.

Therefore:

RESTORATION OF HABITAT ≠ RESTORATION OF EVERY PRIVILEGE

Again:

FACT
≠
CONSEQUENCE
≠
RELATIONSHIP
≠
ACCESS
≠
AUTHORITY


---

XIX. 🏛️ SANCTUARY

A particularly important habitat type emerges:

CONSTITUTIONAL SANCTUARY

A sanctuary is an environment where explicitly protected states, evidence, identities or processes receive additional constitutional constraints.

For example:

SANCTUARY
├── Evidence
├── Memory
├── Identity
└── Protected Process

The sanctuary is not above the Constitution.

It is protected by the Constitution.


---

XX. 💧 MEMORY SANCTUARY

L.A. can therefore contain a protected memory domain:

👑 L.A.
                │
        MEMORY SANCTUARY
                │
             QUAY
                │
          WATERMARKS
                │
             PROOF

The purpose is not secrecy from verification.

The purpose is:

> preventing destructive modification while preserving verifiability.




