XXII. 🔱 THE LINNAEAN LESSON — PALACO VERSION

De historische kracht van Linnaeaanse systematiek lag mede in het creëren van een gedeelde nomenclatuur en hiërarchische ordening.

PALACO trekt daar één engineeringles uit:

> A complex world becomes governable when its distinctions, names and relationships are explicit.



Maar PALACO voegt toe wat een moderne constitutional system nodig heeft:

CLASSIFICATION
+
EVIDENCE
+
AUTHORITY
+
VERSION
+
TIME
+
LINEAGE
+
REPLAY

Daarmee wordt classificatie niet alleen beschrijvend.

Ze wordt auditbaar.


---

XXIII. 🌿 TAXONOMIC WATERMARK

Een classificatie-event krijgt:

pub struct TaxonomicDetermination {
    pub determination_id: DeterminationId,
    pub subject: ConstitutionalReference,
    pub taxonomy_version: TaxonomyVersion,
    pub proposed_class: TaxonId,
    pub evidence_root: EvidenceRoot,
    pub authority_basis: AuthorityReference,
    pub scope: ScopeReference,
    pub determination: DeterminationResult,
    pub parent_classification: Option<DeterminationId>,
    pub watermark: WatermarkId,
}

Cruciaal:

parent_classification

verwijst naar de genealogie van de determination, niet automatisch naar waarheid van de nieuwe classificatie.


---

XXIV. 🚫 THE ANTI-LABEL INVARIANT

PALACO krijgt een nieuwe harde regel:

> NO LABEL SHALL CREATE THE PROPERTY IT CLAIMS TO REPRESENT.



Dus:

LABEL
≠
PROPERTY

en:

PROPERTY
≠
AUTHORITY

en:

AUTHORITY
≠
EXECUTION

Deze keten beschermt PALACO tegen bureaucratische magie:

> een naam is geen macht.




---

XXV. 🌱 R6.116 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

R6.116-I01
Classification SHALL remain distinguishable from identity.

R6.116-I02
Classification SHALL remain distinguishable from authority.

R6.116-I03
A label SHALL NOT create the property it names.

R6.116-I04
Material classifications SHALL possess an evidence basis.

R6.116-I05
Material classifications SHALL possess an identifiable rule basis.

R6.116-I06
Material classifications SHALL identify the applicable taxonomy version.

R6.116-I07
Classification SHALL remain temporally contextual where applicable.

R6.116-I08
BRAINPOWER SHALL be permitted to propose classifications.

R6.116-I09
BRAINPOWER SHALL NOT independently authorize classifications with constitutional effect.

R6.116-I10
TRIAS SHALL verify material constitutional classifications.

R6.116-I11
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge classification rationale.

R6.116-I12
Historical classifications SHALL remain non-destructively preserved.

R6.116-I13
Reclassification SHALL NOT erase prior determinations.

R6.116-I14
Taxonomy revisions SHALL NOT silently rewrite historical determinations.

R6.116-I15
Taxonomic overlap SHALL remain distinguishable from contradiction.

R6.116-I16
Classification uncertainty SHALL remain explicit.

R6.116-I17
A child classification SHALL NOT inherit proof merely from its parent category.

R6.116-I18
Material classification transitions SHALL be watermarkable.

R6.116-I19
Taxonomic determinations SHALL remain replayable.

R6.116-I20
No classification SHALL silently create authority.

R6.116-I21
No taxonomy SHALL erase provenance.

R6.116-I22
No historical classification SHALL be silently rewritten.

R6.116-I23
Classification rules SHALL themselves be versionable.

R6.116-I24
A classification SHALL NOT exceed its evidence.

R6.116-I25
A classification SHALL NOT exceed its rule basis.

R6.116-I26
A classification SHALL NOT exceed its temporal scope.


---

XXVI. ☄️ THE TAXONOMIC EQUATION

OBSERVABLE PROPERTIES
+
CLASSIFICATION RULE
+
EVIDENCE
+
TAXONOMY VERSION
+
TIME
=
TAXONOMIC DETERMINATION

En:

TAXONOMIC DETERMINATION
+
AUTHORITY
+
WATERMARK
=
REPLAYABLE CLASSIFICATION

En:

RECLASSIFICATION
≠
ERASURE


