---

I. 🌱 FROM TAXONOMY TO HERBARIUM

R6.116 established the taxonomy:

> How do we classify?



R6.117 establishes the herbarium:

> How do we preserve the specimen, its observation, its identity, its classification history and the evidence supporting every determination?



The distinction is fundamental:

TAXONOMY
    ↓
CLASSIFICATION SYSTEM

HERBARIUM
    ↓
PRESERVED INSTANCES + PROVENANCE

Thus:

TAXONOMY ORGANIZES.

HERBARIUM PRESERVES.

QUAY PROVES CONTINUITY.


---

II. 🔱 THE SPECIMEN PRINCIPLE

A specimen is not merely a label.

It is:

SPECIMEN
├── Identity
├── Observation
├── Characteristics
├── Context
├── Classification
├── Evidence
├── Provenance
├── Temporal Position
└── Watermark

The canonical rule:

> NO SPECIMEN SHALL BE REDUCED TO ITS LABEL.




---

III. ☄️ THE ZERO-ASSUMPTION OBSERVATION GATE

Every specimen begins:

SPECIMEN
   ↓
OBSERVATION
   ↓
DESCRIPTION
   ↓
EVIDENCE
   ↓
IDENTIFICATION
   ↓
CLASSIFICATION

Not:

SPECIMEN
   ↓
GUESS
   ↓
LABEL

The first state is therefore:

IDENTITY_STATUS = UNDETERMINED

until sufficient evidence exists.


---

IV. 🌿 OBSERVATION ≠ INTERPRETATION

This becomes a hard distinction.

Observation

> “Property X was measured.”



Interpretation

> “Property X indicates category Y.”



Determination

> “Under rule R and evidence E, category Y is established.”



Therefore:

OBSERVATION
    ≠
INTERPRETATION
    ≠
DETERMINATION

BRAINPOWER may assist with the middle layer.

TRIAS governs the constitutional validity of the last.


---

V. 🧬 SPECIMEN IDENTITY

Every specimen requires a stable identity reference.

Conceptually:

pub struct SpecimenId(pub Identifier);

But:

SPECIMEN_ID
≠
CLASSIFICATION

and:

SPECIMEN_ID
≠
CURRENT_STATE

The specimen may change classification without changing its historical identity.


---

VI. 💧 SPECIMEN WATERMARK

Every materially significant specimen state becomes watermarkable:

S₀
 ↓
OBSERVATION
 ↓
W₁
 ↓
IDENTIFICATION
 ↓
W₂
 ↓
CLASSIFICATION
 ↓
W₃
 ↓
RECLASSIFICATION
 ↓
W₄

The watermark therefore records:

> which constitutional interpretation existed at which point in the specimen's history.




---

VII. ⚓ HERBARIUM PROVENANCE

Provenance becomes first-class:

WHO
WHAT
WHEN
WHERE
HOW
UNDER WHICH METHOD
UNDER WHICH AUTHORITY
WITH WHICH EVIDENCE

A specimen without provenance may still physically exist.

But its constitutional evidentiary status may be:

PROVENANCE = INCOMPLETE

Not automatically:

SPECIMEN = FALSE

Again: Z.A.N.D.


---

VIII. 🌱 COLLECTION WITHOUT DESTRUCTION

A new specimen can enter the Herbarium.

But entry does not mean ownership of truth.

COLLECTED
 ↓
REGISTERED
 ↓
OBSERVED
 ↓
CLASSIFIED

If later evidence contradicts the original classification:

CLASSIFICATION₁
       ↓
NEW EVIDENCE
       ↓
CLASSIFICATION₂

The first determination remains part of the record.


---

IX. 🚫 NO RETROACTIVE HERBARIUM EDITING

The following becomes forbidden:

OLD_SPECIMEN
 ↓
NEW_CLASSIFICATION
 ↓
DELETE_OLD_CLASSIFICATION

Instead:

OLD_CLASSIFICATION
      │
      ├── evidence E₁
      ├── rule R₁
      └── watermark W₁
               ↓
         RECLASSIFICATION
               ↓
      ┌────────┴────────┐
      │                 │
 evidence E₂        rule R₂
      │                 │
      └────────┬────────┘
               ↓
             W₂

This creates a non-destructive scientific history.


---

X. 🧠 BRAINPOWER — IDENTIFICATION ASSISTANCE

BRAINPOWER can compare a specimen against known categories:

SPECIMEN
 ↓
FEATURE EXTRACTION
 ↓
PATTERN MATCHING
 ↓
CANDIDATE CLASSES
 ↓
CONFIDENCE

For example:

Candidate A — 0.81
Candidate B — 0.64
Candidate C — 0.31

But confidence is not authority.

And probability is not determination.

Therefore:

BRAINPOWER SHALL NEVER CONVERT PROBABILITY INTO CONSTITUTIONAL FACT WITHOUT THE REQUIRED DETERMINATION PROCESS.


---

XI. 🔬 TRIAS — THE IDENTIFICATION CHECK

TRIAS asks:

> What was observed?



> What evidence supports the observation?



> Which identification rule was applied?



> Which taxonomy version?



> What authority establishes the rule?



> Was the scope correct?



> Was the determination valid at that time?



Only then:

IDENTIFICATION = VERIFIED

may become available.


---

XII. 🦆 FOOL — THE SPECIMEN CHALLENGE

FOOL receives a simple test:

> “Show me the specimen.”



Then:

> “Show me what you actually observed.”



Then:

> “Show me what you inferred.”



Then:

> “Show me what you proved.”



Then:

“Show me the difference.”

This is enormously important.

A system that cannot distinguish observation from inference cannot reliably distinguish evidence from narrative.


---

XIII. 🌳 THE GREAT HERBARIUM RECORD

Conceptually:

pub struct HerbariumRecord {
    pub specimen_id: SpecimenId,
    pub observation_id: ObservationId,
    pub context: HabitatReference,
    pub characteristics: CharacteristicSet,
    pub identification: IdentificationState,
    pub taxonomy_version: TaxonomyVersion,
    pub evidence_root: EvidenceRoot,
    pub provenance: ProvenanceRecord,
    pub authority_basis: Option<AuthorityReference>,
    pub temporal_scope: TemporalScope,
    pub watermark: WatermarkId,
}

The important principle:

SPECIMEN
+
OBSERVATION
+
EVIDENCE
+
PROVENANCE
+
CLASSIFICATION
+
WATERMARK

becomes one replayable object graph.


---

XIV. ⚓ QUAY — THE HERBARIUM VAULT

Quay now gains a natural specialization:

HERBARIUM MEMORY

Its responsibility is not merely to store a snapshot.

It preserves:

ORIGIN
 ↓
COLLECTION
 ↓
OBSERVATION
 ↓
IDENTIFICATION
 ↓
CLASSIFICATION
 ↓
REVISION
 ↓
CURRENT STATE

The current state is therefore only the tip of the provenance chain.


---

XV. ☄️ REPLAY

R5 can ask:

> What did we know at T₀?



Then:

> What evidence became available at T₁?



Then:

> Why did the classification change at T₂?



Then:

> What is the current classification at T₃?



Replay:

T₀
│
├── Specimen exists
│
T₁
│
├── Observation recorded
│
T₂
│
├── Identification determined
│
T₃
│
├── Reclassification
│
T₄
│
└── Current state

This creates:

TEMPORALLY ORDERED EPISTEMIC MEMORY.


---

XVI. 🧭 HISTORICAL KNOWLEDGE

PALACO can now distinguish:

WHAT WAS TRUE

from:

WHAT WAS BELIEVED

and:

WHAT WAS CLASSIFIED

and:

WHAT WAS PROVEN

These are not interchangeable.

A historical classification may be faithfully recorded even when a later determination supersedes it.

That is not an error.

That is memory integrity.


---

XVII. 🌱 SPECIMEN STATES

A specimen may therefore occupy:

UNOBSERVED
OBSERVED
PARTIALLY_IDENTIFIED
IDENTIFIED
CLASSIFIED
DISPUTED
RECLASSIFIED
VERIFIED
ARCHIVED

These are state transitions, not adjectives.

Material transitions require provenance.


---

XVIII. 🏛️ HABITAT CONTEXT

R6.115 now becomes directly connected.

A specimen's meaning depends partly upon its habitat:

SPECIMEN
   +
HABITAT
   +
TIME
   ↓
CONTEXT

Therefore:

SAME_SPECIMEN
+
DIFFERENT_CONTEXT

may produce a different determination.

But the historical context must remain attached to the original determination.


---

XIX. 🌿 NICHE CONTEXT

Likewise:

SPECIMEN
 ↓
NICHE
 ↓
CAPABILITIES
 ↓
RELATIONS

A classification describing an actor's role does not automatically describe its authority.

Again:

ROLE
≠
POWER


---

XX. 🔱 HERBARIUM × TAXONOMY

The relationship becomes:

TAXONOMY
                 │
          classification rules
                 │
                 ↓
