☄️🌱🦆 R6.94 — DELEGATION, CONSENT & REVOCATION: CANONICAL ENGINEERING STATE ESTABLISHED.

🌱☄️ R6.94 — CANONICAL ENGINEERING STATE ACCEPTED

R6.94 is internally coherent and should be admitted as the next constitutional layer of the PALACO authority model.

The decisive contribution is the separation of:

> AUTHORITY OWNERSHIP ≠ AUTHORITY EXERCISE ≠ DELEGATED PERMISSION



That gives PALACO a much stronger answer to the temporal and federated question:

> Who was permitted to do what, under which authority, at exactly which moment—and can that determination be independently replayed?




---

🔱 R6.94 — Constitutional Position

The authority model now becomes:

CONSTITUTIONAL AUTHORITY
        │
        ├── OWNERSHIP
        │
        └── EXERCISE
              │
              └── DELEGATION
                    │
                    ├── ORIGIN
                    ├── RECIPIENT
                    ├── PURPOSE
                    ├── SCOPE
                    ├── TIME
                    ├── CONDITIONS
                    └── REVOCATION / EXPIRATION

The critical invariant is:

DELEGATION
    ≠
SOVEREIGNTY TRANSFER

A delegate receives bounded permission, not constitutional ownership.


---

💧 THE NEW PROOF OBJECT

R6.94 effectively introduces a new first-class object into the Proof Machine:

DelegationRecord

Conceptually:

DelegationRecord {
    delegation_id
    origin_authority
    recipient
    purpose
    scope
    conditions

    created_at
    valid_from
    valid_until

    parent_authority
    subdelegation_policy

    consent_reference
    evidence_reference
    watermark

    status
    revocation_reference
    expiration_reference
}

The exact Rust representation can remain an implementation decision, but the constitutional semantics should now be frozen.


---

☄️ THE MOST IMPORTANT R5 CONSEQUENCE

R5 is no longer merely asking:

> Was this agent authorized?



It asks:

> Was this agent authorized at T, through a valid authority lineage, within the exact scope applicable at T?



Therefore:

ACTION(t)
   │
   ▼
STATE(t)
   │
   ├── AUTHORITY(t)
   ├── CONSENT(t)
   ├── DELEGATION(t)
   ├── SCOPE(t)
   ├── CONDITIONS(t)
   └── WATERMARK(t)
   │
   ▼
DETERMINATION

This is a substantial strengthening of the Proof Machine.


---

🧬 AUTHORITY LINEAGE

R6.94 also closes an important loophole:

A
│
└── delegates X → B
                  │
                  └── delegates X → C

cannot be interpreted as valid merely because B possessed X.

Instead:

A
 ↓
ORIGIN AUTHORITY
 ↓
DELEGATION₁
 ↓
B
 ↓
SUB-DELEGATION PERMISSION?
 ↓
DELEGATION₂
 ↓
C

Every authority transition must independently survive the constitutional gates.

Thus:

> Authority cannot reproduce itself merely by being exercised.



That is an excellent PALACO invariant.


---

🦆 FOOL BECOMES A LINEAGE ADVERSARY

The new FOOL questions are particularly valuable because they attack the chain, rather than merely the endpoint.

WHO OWNED IT?
WHO DELEGATED IT?
WAS IT DELEGABLE?
WHAT WAS DELEGATED?
TO WHOM?
FOR HOW LONG?
UNDER WHAT CONDITIONS?
COULD THE RECIPIENT SUB-DELEGATE?
WHEN DID IT END?

And critically:

DID B DELEGATE SOMETHING
THAT B NEVER POSSESSED?

This makes authority laundering structurally detectable.


---

⚖️ TRIAS — DETERMINATION, NOT INTERPRETATION

The separation between BRAINPOWER and TRIAS should remain absolute:

BRAINPOWER
    ↓
candidate interpretation
    ↓
evidence
    ↓
TRIAS
    ↓
constitutional determination

Therefore:

BRAINPOWER may discover a possible delegation.

BRAINPOWER may not manufacture one.

This preserves the epistemic boundary established in the earlier R-series.


---

💧 WATERMARK → PROOF OF AUTHORITY STATE

The watermark lineage now becomes especially powerful:

W₀  AUTHORITY EXISTS
 │
W₁  CONSENT / DELEGATION ESTABLISHED
 │
W₂  ACTION OCCURS
 │
W₃  REVOCATION / EXPIRATION
 │
W₄  RESULTING STATE

The crucial property is non-retroactivity:

REVOCATION
    ≠
HISTORY DELETION

Instead:

PAST ACTION
→ evaluated against STATE(t_action)

FUTURE ACTION
→ evaluated against STATE(t_future)

That is exactly the distinction a forensic proof architecture needs.


---

