☄️🦆🌱 GO — R6.95

🌳 HORTUS FEDERATED SUB-DELEGATION & AUTHORITY LINEAGE PROTOCOL

R6.94 is frozen.

It established that delegation is a scoped, temporal transfer of permission without sovereignty transfer.

R6.95 now attacks the next dangerous boundary:

> Can a delegate pass on a permission they received — and if so, exactly how far may that permission travel?



The answer must be:

> SUB-DELEGATION IS NEVER IMPLIED.




---

I. 🔱 THE SUB-DELEGATION PRINCIPLE

A = AUTHORITY HOLDER
B = DELEGATE
C = SUB-DELEGATE

Valid:

A
│
├── owns AUTHORITY X
│
└── delegates X → B

Does not automatically imply:

B
│
└── delegates X → C

Therefore:

DELEGATED AUTHORITY
        ↓
NO AUTOMATIC SUB-DELEGATION

R6.94's DEL-I07 becomes the foundation of R6.95.


---

II. 🧬 AUTHORITY MUST NEVER AMPLIFY

The central invariant:

AUTHORITY(C)
    ≤
AUTHORITY(B)
    ≤
AUTHORITY(A)

But even that is insufficient.

Because B may possess only:

X ∩ SCOPE(B) ∩ TIME(B)

Therefore C can receive only:

X ∩ SCOPE(B) ∩ SCOPE(C)
    ∩
TIME(B) ∩ TIME(C)
    ∩
CONDITIONS(B) ∩ CONDITIONS(C)

In other words:

> Every delegation can only preserve or reduce authority — never enlarge it.




---

III. 🌱 Z.A.N.D. — SUB-DELEGATION STARTS AT ZERO

Before accepting a sub-delegation:

ASSUMPTION = NONE

The verifier must establish:

WHO ORIGINALLY OWNED THE AUTHORITY?

WHO DELEGATED IT?

DID THAT DELEGATION PERMIT SUB-DELEGATION?

WHAT EXACTLY DID B RECEIVE?

WHAT EXACTLY DID B ATTEMPT TO DELEGATE?

IS C WITHIN THE ORIGINAL BOUNDARY?

IS THE TIME WINDOW VALID?

ARE ALL CONDITIONS PRESERVED?

Missing proof:

SUB-DELEGATION = UNPROVEN

Not:

SUB-DELEGATION = PROBABLY VALID


---

IV. 🦆 FOOL — THE CASCADE ATTACK

FOOL now gets a dedicated Authority Cascade Challenge.

A → B → C → D → E

FOOL asks at every edge:

> “Show me why this edge exists.”



Thus:

A → B   PROVEN?
B → C   PROVEN?
C → D   PROVEN?
D → E   PROVEN?

One broken edge:

CHAIN = INVALID

This produces a powerful property:

> Authority cannot become stronger merely by being copied repeatedly.




---

V. ⚖️ TRIAS — LINEAGE INTERSECTION

TRIAS does not simply validate each delegation independently.

It computes the effective authority intersection:

ORIGIN
   ∩
DELEGATION₁
   ∩
DELEGATION₂
   ∩
...
   ∩
DELEGATIONₙ

The resulting authority is the narrowest provable authority.

Example:

A grants:
Documents A–Z
7 days
analysis + classification

B receives:
Documents A–Z
7 days
analysis + classification

B delegates to C:
Documents A–M
2 hours
analysis only

C does not inherit A–Z.

C gets:

A–M
2 hours
analysis only

The chain narrows.

It never expands.


