XIV. 🔒 R6.95 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

DEL-S01

Sub-delegation SHALL NOT be implied.

DEL-S02

A delegate SHALL NOT delegate authority exceeding its own authority.

DEL-S03

Sub-delegation SHALL require explicit constitutional permission.

DEL-S04

Every sub-delegation SHALL identify its immediate parent delegation.

DEL-S05

Every sub-delegation SHALL preserve originating provenance.

DEL-S06

Effective authority SHALL NOT expand through delegation depth.

DEL-S07

Scope SHALL be monotonically non-expanding through delegation chains.

DEL-S08

Temporal validity SHALL be monotonically non-expanding through delegation chains.

DEL-S09

Conditions imposed by an originating authority SHALL propagate unless explicitly and constitutionally superseded.

DEL-S10

Revocation of a parent authority SHALL invalidate derived authority unless an independently valid authority basis exists.

DEL-S11

Historical sub-delegations SHALL remain replayable.

DEL-S12

Every material sub-delegation SHALL be watermarkable.

DEL-S13

FOOL SHALL be able to challenge every delegation edge.

DEL-S14

TRIAS SHALL validate the complete authority lineage.

DEL-S15

BRAINPOWER SHALL NOT independently authorize sub-delegation.

DEL-S16

Cross-Citadel sub-delegation SHALL preserve both originating and receiving provenance.

DEL-S17

Federation membership SHALL NOT itself authorize sub-delegation.

DEL-S18

A broken lineage edge SHALL prevent constitutional authorization of the derived action.

DEL-S19

Delegation depth SHALL NOT create additional constitutional authority.

DEL-S20

Historical validity SHALL be determined according to the authority state applicable at execution time.


