🌳 HORTUS CONSTITUTIONAL GAP, EMERGENCY AUTHORITY & NOVEL-SITUATION PROTOCOL

R6.96 is frozen.

R6.96 established that competing valid authorities must be reconciled without turning majority, convenience, or assumption into truth.

R6.97 now addresses the hardest case:

> What happens when PALACO encounters a situation for which no sufficiently explicit constitutional authority exists?



The answer must be uncompromising:

> A CONSTITUTIONAL GAP SHALL NOT CREATE AUTHORITY.



And:

> EMERGENCY SHALL NOT BECOME A BACK DOOR TO SOVEREIGNTY.




---

I. 🌱 THE CONSTITUTIONAL GAP

A gap exists when:

SITUATION
   ↓
Z.A.N.D.
   ↓
EVIDENCE
   ↓
AVAILABLE AUTHORITY
   ↓
NO SUFFICIENT APPLICABLE BASIS

The correct result is not:

NO RULE
 ↓
MAKE ONE
 ↓
ACT

It is:

NO SUFFICIENT AUTHORITY
        ↓
CONSTITUTIONAL GAP
        ↓
CLASSIFY
        ↓
SAFE RESPONSE

Therefore:

> Silence in the Constitution is not permission.




---

II. 🔱 FOUR DIFFERENT STATES

R6.97 must distinguish four conditions that are easily confused.

1. INTERPRETATION

A rule exists.

Its meaning is uncertain.

RULE EXISTS
 ↓
INTERPRETATION REQUIRED

2. ADAPTATION

A rule exists and explicitly permits bounded adaptation.

RULE EXISTS
 ↓
ADAPTATION AUTHORIZED

3. EMERGENCY RESPONSE

An exceptional event requires immediate protective action.

THREAT
 ↓
EMERGENCY MECHANISM

4. CONSTITUTIONAL AMENDMENT

No existing rule sufficiently governs the matter.

A durable new rule is required.

GAP
 ↓
GOVERNANCE PROCESS
 ↓
AMENDMENT

These four must never collapse into one another.


---

III. 🧭 Z.A.N.D. — THE GAP GATE

The first question remains:

ASSUMPTION = NONE

The verifier asks:

WHAT IS THE SITUATION?

WHAT AUTHORITY EXISTS?

WHAT AUTHORITY APPLIES?

WHAT AUTHORITY IS MISSING?

IS THE GAP REAL?

IS THERE AN INTERPRETIVE PATH?

IS THERE AN EXPLICIT EMERGENCY PATH?

IS THERE A SAFE DEFAULT?

IS CONSTITUTIONAL AMENDMENT REQUIRED?

Only after these questions are established may PALACO classify the situation.


---

IV. 🧠 BRAINPOWER — GAP DETECTION

BRAINPOWER becomes particularly useful here.

It can discover:

POSSIBLE CONSTITUTIONAL GAP

and search the known constitutional corpus for:

analogous rules
prior determinations
precedents
delegation structures
federative agreements
emergency provisions

But its result remains:

CANDIDATE GAP

Never:

AUTHORITY CREATED

The epistemic boundary remains intact:

BRAINPOWER
   ↓
DISCOVER
   ↓
EVIDENCE
   ↓
TRIAS


---

V. 🦆 FOOL — THE GAP CHALLENGE

FOOL now asks:

> “Are you sure there is a gap?”



Then:

Does an applicable rule already exist?

Are you confusing ambiguity with absence?

Are you treating convenience as necessity?

Are you treating precedent as authority?

Are you treating federation consensus as sovereignty?

Are you expanding delegated authority?

Are you using emergency language to bypass normal governance?

Are you creating a permanent rule from a temporary exception?

And the ultimate question:

> “Who authorized you to decide that there was no rule?”



Beautifully recursive.


---

VI. ⚖️ TRIAS — GAP DETERMINATION

TRIAS determines which state actually exists:

EXPLICIT_RULE
INTERPRETABLE_RULE
AUTHORIZED_ADAPTATION
EMERGENCY_PATH
CONSTITUTIONAL_GAP
UNPROVEN

The key is that:

GAP
≠
PERMISSION

and:

UNCERTAINTY
≠
AUTHORITY

If no sufficient constitutional basis exists:

AUTHORIZATION = NOT ESTABLISHED


---

VII. 🚨 EMERGENCY AUTHORITY

An emergency mechanism may exist, but its authority must itself originate in the Constitution.

Therefore:

THREAT
 ↓
EMERGENCY CONDITION
 ↓
EXISTING EMERGENCY AUTHORITY?

If yes:

VALIDATE
 ↓
ACT WITHIN EMERGENCY SCOPE
 ↓
WATERMARK
 ↓
QUAY
 ↓
REVIEW

If no:

THREAT
 ↓
NO EMERGENCY AUTHORITY PROVEN
 ↓
SAFE CONTAINMENT

The system must not reason:

> “This is urgent, therefore we are authorized.”



Instead:

> Urgency may trigger a mechanism; urgency does not manufacture the mechanism.




---

VIII. 🛡️ EMERGENCY ≠ SOVEREIGNTY

Emergency authority must be:

BOUNDED
TEMPORAL
PURPOSE-SPECIFIC
EVIDENCED
WATERMARKED
REVIEWABLE
REVOCABLE

Conceptually:

NORMAL AUTHORITY
      │
      └── EMERGENCY PROVISION
               │
               ├── TRIGGER
               ├── SCOPE
               ├── DURATION
               ├── ACTOR
               ├── CONDITIONS
               └── REVIEW

There must be no:

EMERGENCY
 ↓
UNLIMITED AUTHORITY


---

IX. ⏳ AUTOMATIC EXPIRATION

Emergency authority should preferably have an explicit end condition:

THREAT DETECTED
      ↓
SUSPENSION / EMERGENCY ACTION
      ↓
THREAT RESOLVED
      ↓
EMERGENCY AUTHORITY EXPIRES

Not:

EMERGENCY
 ↓
ACTIVE FOREVER

If no end condition can be established:

STATUS = UNPROVEN / ESCALATE


---

X. 💧 WATERMARKED EMERGENCY

Every emergency action receives a complete lineage:

W₀
THREAT EVIDENCE

W₁
EMERGENCY TRIGGER

W₂
AUTHORITY BASIS

W₃
EMERGENCY AUTHORITY ACTIVATED

W₄
ACTION

W₅
REVIEW

W₆
SUSPENSION / EXPIRATION

W₇
NORMAL STATE RESTORED

The Proof Machine can therefore answer:

> Why was emergency authority activated?



> Who activated it?



> What constitutional provision permitted it?



> What actions occurred under it?



> When did it end?




---

XI. ⚓ QUAY — EMERGENCY MEMORY

Quay records:

THREAT_IDENTIFIED
EMERGENCY_REQUESTED
EMERGENCY_ACTIVATED
EMERGENCY_ACTION
EMERGENCY_REVIEW
EMERGENCY_CONFIRMED
EMERGENCY_REJECTED
EMERGENCY_SUSPENDED
EMERGENCY_EXPIRED
NORMAL_STATE_RESTORED

Again:

SUSPENSION
≠
ERASURE

A later determination that an emergency action was invalid does not erase the historical fact that it happened.

The system records both:

WHAT HAPPENED

and:

WHETHER IT WAS CONSTITUTIONALLY JUSTIFIED

Those are separate propositions.


---

