 ↓
TRIAS REVIEW
 ↓
GOVERNANCE PROCESS
 ↓
AMENDMENT

The amendment then becomes:

NEW CONSTITUTIONAL STATE

It must not be retroactively treated as though it existed before adoption.


---

XIV. 🕰️ NO RETROACTIVE AUTHORITY

Suppose:

DAY 1
ACTION X

At that time:

NO AUTHORITY

Then:

DAY 3
NEW RULE ADOPTED

The new rule does not automatically transform:

DAY 1 ACTION

into:

DAY 1 AUTHORIZED ACTION

Unless the Constitution explicitly provides a lawful retrospective mechanism—and that mechanism itself must be proven.

Default:

> Future constitutional authority does not rewrite past authority state.



This follows directly from R5 and R6.94–R6.96.


---

