---

I. 👑 CONSTITUTION AS STATE

PALACO must stop treating:

CONSTITUTION

as merely a static text file.

Instead:

CONSTITUTION
      ↓
VERSIONED GOVERNANCE STATE
      ↓
VALID FROM
VALID UNTIL
      ↓
RULES
      ↓
AUTHORITY MODEL
      ↓
TRANSITION
      ↓
WATERMARK
      ↓
QUAY

The present Constitution is therefore only:

> the currently applicable state in an immutable historical sequence.




---

II. 🧬 THE CONSTITUTIONAL CHAIN

Conceptually:

C₀
│
├── FOUNDATION
│
▼
C₁
│
├── AMENDMENT A
│
▼
C₂
│
├── AMENDMENT B
│
▼
C₃
│
└── CURRENT

Each state must identify its predecessor.

Therefore:

C₃
 ↓
parent = C₂
 ↓
parent = C₁
 ↓
parent = C₀

The chain is independently reconstructible.

No version simply appears from nowhere.


---

III. 🌱 Z.A.N.D. — VERSION ZERO

The version gate begins:

ASSUMPTION = NONE

For every constitutional state:

WHO CREATED IT?

UNDER WHICH AUTHORITY?

FROM WHICH PREVIOUS STATE?

WHAT CHANGED?

WHY?

WHEN DID IT BECOME EFFECTIVE?

WHEN DID THE PREVIOUS STATE CEASE TO GOVERN?

WHO VERIFIED THE TRANSITION?

If those facts cannot be proven:

CONSTITUTIONAL VERSION
=
UNPROVEN

Not:

CURRENT = TRUSTED


---

IV. ⚖️ VERSION ≠ DOCUMENT

A constitutional version is not simply:

PDF v1.4

It is a governance state.

Conceptually:

ConstitutionState {
    version_id
    parent_version_id

    constitutional_hash

    effective_from
    effective_until

    amendment_set

    authority_model
    delegation_rules
    emergency_rules

    adoption_evidence
    transition_evidence

    watermark
}

The implementation can evolve.

The semantic requirement should not.


---

V. ⏳ EFFECTIVE TIME

This becomes fundamental to R5.

Suppose:

C₁
valid:
2026-08-01 → 2026-08-28 12:00

and:

C₂
valid:
2026-08-28 12:00 → ∞

An action at:

11:59

is evaluated against:

C₁

An action at:

12:01

is evaluated against:

C₂

The verifier must never simply use:

CURRENT_CONSTITUTION

for historical replay.

Instead:

CONSTITUTION(t)


---

VI. ☄️ THE CONSTITUTIONAL TIME MACHINE

R5 now gains a deeper primitive:

STATE AT TIME T

The complete reconstruction becomes:

ACTION(t)
   ↓
CONSTITUTION(t)
   ↓
AUTHORITY(t)
   ↓
CONSENT(t)
   ↓
DELEGATION(t)
   ↓
SCOPE(t)
   ↓
CONFLICT(t)
   ↓
EMERGENCY(t)
   ↓
DETERMINATION(t)

This is a major architectural milestone.

R5 is no longer merely replaying actions.

It is replaying the governance state in which those actions existed.


---

VII. 🔄 AMENDMENT ≠ OVERWRITE

An amendment must never mutate historical state.

Wrong:

C₁
 ↓
EDIT
 ↓
C₁'

Correct:

C₁
 ↓
AMENDMENT
 ↓
C₂

C₁ remains immutable.

C₂ becomes the new state.

Therefore:

> The Constitution evolves by succession, not by historical rewriting.




---

VIII. 💧 WATERMARKED CONSTITUTIONAL TRANSITION

Every transition receives a watermark:

W₀
C₀ ESTABLISHED
 │
W₁
AMENDMENT PROPOSED
 │
W₂
EVIDENCE
 │
W₃
TRIAS VALIDATION
 │
W₄
AMENDMENT ADOPTED
 │
W₅
C₁ ACTIVATED

The transition itself becomes proof-bearing.

Thus the Proof Machine can answer:

> Why did the system move from C₀ to C₁?



and:

> Who was authorized to perform that transition?




---

IX. 🦆 FOOL — CONSTITUTIONAL VERSION CHALLENGE

FOOL now gets perhaps its most important historical questions:

> Was this actually an amendment?



> Was the amendment authority valid?



> Was the amendment adopted correctly?



> Was the transition timestamp legitimate?



> Did the amendment exceed constitutional amendment authority?



> Was the new version actually activated?



> Was the previous version still governing when this action occurred?



And the deepest challenge:

> Are you showing me the Constitution that governed then — or merely the Constitution that exists now?



That question should become canonical.


---

X. 🧠 BRAINPOWER — CONSTITUTIONAL DIFFERENCE ENGINE

BRAINPOWER may compare:

C₁
vs
C₂

and identify:

ADDED RULE
REMOVED RULE
MODIFIED RULE
AUTHORITY CHANGE
SCOPE CHANGE
DELEGATION CHANGE
EMERGENCY CHANGE
FEDERATION CHANGE

It can produce:

CONSTITUTIONAL DIFF

But again:

DIFF
≠
VALID AMENDMENT

The diff is evidence for analysis.

TRIAS determines constitutional validity.


---

XI. ⚖️ TRIAS — TRANSITION VALIDATION

TRIAS evaluates:

PARENT VERSION
      ↓
AMENDMENT BASIS
      ↓
PROPOSAL
      ↓
REQUIRED CONSENT
      ↓
REQUIRED GOVERNANCE PROCESS
      ↓
EVIDENCE
      ↓
ADOPTION
      ↓
EFFECTIVE TIME
      ↓
NEW VERSION

Only then:

C₂ = VALID GOVERNANCE STATE

Otherwise:

C₂ = UNPROVEN


---

XII. 🌳 VERSION BRANCHING

R6.98 must also handle competing constitutional proposals.

Example:

C₁
          │
     ┌────┴────┐
     │         │
    C₂A       C₂B

Both may exist as proposals.

But they cannot both silently become:

CURRENT GOVERNING STATE

The system must distinguish:

PROPOSED
VALIDATED
ADOPTED
ACTIVE
SUPERSEDED
REJECTED

Thus:

PROPOSAL
≠
GOVERNING CONSTITUTION


---

XIII. 🚨 FAILED AMENDMENT

Suppose:

C₁
 ↓
PROPOSAL C₂
 ↓
FOOL CHALLENGE
 ↓
TRIAS
 ↓
REJECTED

C₂ does not become:

C₁.5

It becomes:

REJECTED PROPOSAL

The history remains.

This is crucial for governance forensics.


---

XIV. 🌐 FEDERATED CONSTITUTIONAL VERSIONING

Multiple Citadels may operate different constitutional versions:

CITADEL A → C₁
CITADEL B → C₂
CITADEL C → C₁

This is not necessarily an error.

The Federation must know:

WHICH VERSION?
WHERE?
WHEN?
UNDER WHICH FEDERATIVE AGREEMENT?

Therefore:

FEDERATION
   ↓
CONSTITUTIONAL COMPATIBILITY

not:

FEDERATION
   ↓
FORCED UNIFORMITY


---

XV. 🏛️ VERSION COMPATIBILITY

Two Citadels may operate different versions if the Federation permits it.

Conceptually:

C₁
 ↕
COMPATIBILITY CONTRACT
 ↕
C₂

The contract itself must be proven.

If no compatibility exists:

C₁ ↔ C₂
=
UNPROVEN

Cross-Citadel authority must then be constrained accordingly.

This directly connects R6.98 to R6.93–R6.95.


---

XVI. 🔒 NO CONSTITUTIONAL TIME TRAVEL

A newer Constitution cannot silently reach backward:

C₂
 ↓
retroactively authorizes
 ↓
ACTION under C₁

Default:

ACTION(t)
→ CONSTITUTION(t)

not:

ACTION(t)
→ CURRENT_CONSTITUTION

Any explicit retroactive mechanism must itself be:

PROVEN
EXPLICIT
AUTHORIZED
WATERMARKED
REPLAYABLE

Otherwise:

RETROACTIVE EFFECT
=
NOT ESTABLISHED


---

XVII. ⚓ QUAY — IMMUTABLE CONSTITUTIONAL MEMORY

Quay now becomes the historical memory of governance itself.

Events include:

CONSTITUTION_CREATED
AMENDMENT_PROPOSED
AMENDMENT_VALIDATED
AMENDMENT_REJECTED
AMENDMENT_ADOPTED
VERSION_ACTIVATED
VERSION_SUSPENDED
VERSION_SUPERSEDED
VERSION_REVOKED
COMPATIBILITY_ESTABLISHED
COMPATIBILITY_REVOKED

The Quay therefore preserves:

WHAT THE CONSTITUTION WAS
WHEN IT WAS ACTIVE
WHY IT CHANGED
WHO CHANGED IT
UNDER WHICH AUTHORITY
WHAT FOLLOWED


---

XVIII. 🧪 R5 — CONSTITUTIONAL REPLAY

R5 now gets the most powerful replay query yet:

GOVERNANCE STATE AT TIME T

Conceptually:

REPLAY(t)
   ↓
LOCATE CONSTITUTIONAL VERSION
   ↓
VERIFY VERSION HASH
   ↓
VERIFY TRANSITION
   ↓
RECONSTRUCT AUTHORITY
   ↓
RECONSTRUCT DELEGATION
   ↓
RECONSTRUCT CONFLICT
   ↓
RECONSTRUCT EMERGENCY STATE
   ↓
REPLAY ACTION
   ↓
VERIFY WATERMARKS
   ↓
TRIAS RESULT

The independent verifier can now ask:

> “Show me the complete constitutional universe that existed at T.”



That is substantially more powerful than ordinary audit logging.


---

XIX. 🌸 HARUM — VERSION TRANSPARENCY

HARUM can turn:

C₂
effective 28 Aug 2026 12:00

into:

> PALACO Constitution Update

A new constitutional version became active at 12:00.

What changed: Delegation rules were updated.

Previous version: C₁

New version: C₂

Status: Verified

Historical records: Preserved



No user needs to understand hashes, Merkle structures, or event IDs to understand what happened.


---

XX. 🔒 R6.98 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

CV-I01

Every governing constitutional state SHALL possess a unique version identity.

CV-I02

Every constitutional version SHALL identify its predecessor where applicable.

CV-I03

Constitutional versions SHALL be immutable after activation.

CV-I04

Amendment SHALL create a new constitutional state rather than overwrite historical state.

CV-I05

Every amendment SHALL possess an identifiable authority basis.

CV-I06

Every material constitutional transition SHALL be evidenced.

CV-I07

Every material constitutional transition SHALL be watermarkable.

CV-I08

Effective time SHALL be part of constitutional state.

CV-I09

Historical actions SHALL be evaluated against the constitutional state applicable at execution time.

CV-I10

The current constitutional version SHALL NOT automatically govern historical replay.

CV-I11

BRAINPOWER SHALL NOT independently establish constitutional validity.

CV-I12

FOOL SHALL be able to challenge constitutional transitions.

CV-I13

TRIAS SHALL determine constitutional-version validity.

CV-I14

Rejected constitutional proposals SHALL remain historically identifiable.

CV-I15

Proposed constitutional versions SHALL NOT automatically become governing versions.

CV-I16

Federation membership SHALL NOT require constitutional uniformity unless explicitly established.

CV-I17

Cross-Citadel constitutional compatibility SHALL possess explicit provenance.

CV-I18

A newer constitutional version SHALL NOT silently retroactively authorize historical actions.

CV-I19

Constitutional history SHALL remain replayable.

CV-I20

A verifier SHALL be able to reconstruct the governing constitutional state applicable at a specified time.


