XXIII. 🌱 THE R6.98 PRINCIPLE

> A Constitution may change without changing what the Constitution was.



And:

> Governance evolves by creating new states, not by rewriting old ones.



And therefore:

> Every constitutional action must be evaluated against the constitutional state that actually governed at that time.



This creates an exceptionally strong temporal foundation for PALACO.


